cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Policy Knowledge Graph Explorer: a multi-model semantic knowledge graph
  for exploring environmental governance corpora (v2, 191-document corpus)
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Barry
    family-names: Johnston
    affiliation: Atlantic Technological University
    ORCID: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5287-2287'
  - given-names: James
    family-names: Moran
    affiliation: Atlantic Technological University
    ORCID: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2845-4325'
abstract: >-
  An interactive knowledge-graph tool that maps the semantic relationships
  across a corpus of 191 Irish, EU and international environmental-governance
  documents. Documents are segmented into ~350-word passages, embedded with a
  three-model ensemble (BGE-M3, Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B and MiniLM) combined by
  similarity-matrix averaging, and assembled into a document-level similarity
  graph. Connection strength is calibrated non-parametrically against the
  corpus's own background distribution. The output is a single standalone,
  client-side application with linked 2D network, 3D orbit and heatmap views
  and a reference-datum mode. Status: research / decision-support tool;
  similarity measures thematic overlap, not agreement or legal consistency.
keywords:
  - text embeddings
  - knowledge graphs
  - environmental policy
  - document similarity
  - policy coherence
  - information visualisation
  - natural language processing
